<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>RFI - All the news from France, Europe, Africa and the rest of the world.</title><description>Follow any political information, cultural, sporting and live streaming on RFI. The latest information, news and events around the world.</description><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/</link><lastBuildDate>Tue, 11 Aug 2026 13:30:37 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.rfi.fr/en/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>International</category><title>Former Syrian leader Assad sentenced to death in absentia over war crimes</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260811-former-syrian-leader-assad-sentenced-to-death-in-absentia-over-war-crimes</link><description>
A Syrian court on Tuesday sentenced former ruler Bashar al-Assad to death after a trial in absentia, convicting him of atrocities committed during the country's civil war. Six of his closest aides were also handed death sentences.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/6c74b05a-88a3-11f0-b62a-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-48VX9PL.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/6c74b05a-88a3-11f0-b62a-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-48VX9PL.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">73c8abca-956f-11f1-aff4-e70fbbb452ac</guid><pubDate>Tue, 11 Aug 2026 11:58:12 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/6c74b05a-88a3-11f0-b62a-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-48VX9PL.jpg">AFP - LOUAI BESHARA</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>France and EU join international aid effort after Colombia earthquake</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260811-france-eu-join-international-aid-effort-after-colombia-earthquake</link><description>
France has joined the European Union and a host of countries in offering assistance to Colombia, where volunteers and rescuers are searching for survivors following Monday's deadly earthquake.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/928cf576-9555-11f1-afcb-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C4CQ8V6.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/928cf576-9555-11f1-afcb-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C4CQ8V6.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8e96a684-955e-11f1-bebd-75c492606bc4</guid><pubDate>Tue, 11 Aug 2026 10:08:10 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/928cf576-9555-11f1-afcb-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C4CQ8V6.jpg">© Jamie Saldarriaga / AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Rebel forces in Ethiopia's Tigray state condemn army drone strikes</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260811-rebel-forces-in-ethiopia-s-tigray-state-condemn-army-drone-strikes</link><description>
Rebel authorities on Tuesday accused the Ethiopian government of carrying out deadly drone strikes in southern Tigray state and condemned the move as "a serious escalation", amid fears of a new war. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/de06147a-1d45-11f1-a5b3-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/tigray-afp-march-2026-000-A26B6PM.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/de06147a-1d45-11f1-a5b3-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/tigray-afp-march-2026-000-A26B6PM.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b05c8bea-9567-11f1-8107-913aa69e7026</guid><pubDate>Tue, 11 Aug 2026 13:25:14 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/de06147a-1d45-11f1-a5b3-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/tigray-afp-march-2026-000-A26B6PM.jpg">AFP - ABEL GEREZGIHER</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>May ’68 protest leader Cohn-Bendit pledges support to Glucksmann for 2027</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260810-may-68-veteran-cohn-bendit-throws-support-behind-left-wing-glucksmann-for-2027</link><description>
Former Green MEP Daniel Cohn-Bendit, a historic figure on the French left, on Monday gave his support to Raphaël Glucksmann for France’s 2027 presidential election, in an interview with Le Point magazine.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/28fea318-5836-11f1-af93-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B3TU2CY.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/28fea318-5836-11f1-af93-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B3TU2CY.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a90b0ffe-94b5-11f1-ba5c-c57808d5257e</guid><pubDate>Mon, 10 Aug 2026 13:00:11 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/28fea318-5836-11f1-af93-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B3TU2CY.jpg">AFP - LOU BENOIST</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>France introduces tough fines for unsolicited telemarketing calls</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260811-france-introduces-tough-fines-for-unsolicited-telemarketing-calls</link><description>
France has banned unsolicited telemarketing calls under a new law to protect consumers and shield vulnerable people from fraudulent commercial practices. Individuals who make illegal calls can be fined up to €75,000 per call when the new law comes into effect on Tuesday.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/597fa4c2-3723-11f0-b8ae-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/%D1%81%D0%BF%D0%B0%D0%BC-%D0%B4%D0%B7%D0%B2%D1%96%D0%BD%D0%BA%D0%B8.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/597fa4c2-3723-11f0-b8ae-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/%D1%81%D0%BF%D0%B0%D0%BC-%D0%B4%D0%B7%D0%B2%D1%96%D0%BD%D0%BA%D0%B8.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0696e0c0-93f4-11f1-b693-771bd1b13781</guid><pubDate>Tue, 11 Aug 2026 05:56:53 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/597fa4c2-3723-11f0-b8ae-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/%D1%81%D0%BF%D0%B0%D0%BC-%D0%B4%D0%B7%D0%B2%D1%96%D0%BD%D0%BA%D0%B8.jpg">© Michael Sohn / AP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Moscow and Damascus reach deal over Russian military bases in Syria</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260810-moscow-and-damascus-reach-deal-over-russian-military-bases-in-syria</link><description>
Syria said on Sunday it had reached a deal with Moscow on the fate of Russia's two bases in the country, which it once used to provide military support to ousted leader Bashar al-Assad during the Syrian civil war.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7b02e676-151a-11ea-9ffb-005056a99247/w:1024/p:16x9/2015-10-23T202154Z_1487561120_GF20000030015_RTRMADP_3_MIDEAST-CRISIS-SYRIA-RUSSIA.JPG"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7b02e676-151a-11ea-9ffb-005056a99247/w:1024/p:16x9/2015-10-23T202154Z_1487561120_GF20000030015_RTRMADP_3_MIDEAST-CRISIS-SYRIA-RUSSIA.JPG" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">67a3afc4-9476-11f1-b20d-ffc054c909af</guid><pubDate>Mon, 10 Aug 2026 04:56:38 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7b02e676-151a-11ea-9ffb-005056a99247/w:1024/p:16x9/2015-10-23T202154Z_1487561120_GF20000030015_RTRMADP_3_MIDEAST-CRISIS-SYRIA-RUSSIA.JPG">REUTERS</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Iran says ‘Muslim Nato’ pact reflects retreat from US security umbrella</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260810-iran-says-muslim-nato-pact-reflects-retreat-from-us-security-umbrella</link><description>
Tehran has played down concerns over a new mutual defence pact between Saudi Arabia, Turkey and Pakistan, while portraying the agreement as evidence of declining regional reliance on the United States.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c1bf5a5a-92df-11f1-83b4-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C47Q664.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c1bf5a5a-92df-11f1-83b4-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C47Q664.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">505d03ae-94b9-11f1-840e-457ddd2c08ca</guid><pubDate>Mon, 10 Aug 2026 15:21:58 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c1bf5a5a-92df-11f1-83b4-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C47Q664.jpg">© AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Record temperatures swept regions home to 900 million people in July</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260810-record-temperatures-swept-regions-home-to-900-million-people-in-july</link><description>
Regions home to around 900 million people experienced their hottest July on record in 2026, including areas in the Sahel, Central America, France and Spain, according to analysis of Copernicus data.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/9d44235c-9499-11f1-bf58-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/3e6a1923f4e3906b09abf7fceee922f9e28476bb.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/9d44235c-9499-11f1-bf58-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/3e6a1923f4e3906b09abf7fceee922f9e28476bb.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">13fd717a-949e-11f1-84b4-d34b2a11c752</guid><pubDate>Mon, 10 Aug 2026 09:33:33 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/9d44235c-9499-11f1-bf58-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/3e6a1923f4e3906b09abf7fceee922f9e28476bb.jpg">© Ina FASSBENDER / AFP/File</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Ghana backs Jamaica's petition to push UK for slavery reparations</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260810-monday-o-n-ghana-backs-jamaica-s-petition-to-push-uk-for-slavery-reparations</link><description>
Jamaica and Ghana, both former British colonies subjected to the transatlantic slave trade, are presenting a united front in the drive for reparatory justice. As Kingston prepares to lodge a formal petition with King Charles III seeking to advance its claim for reparations from the United Kingdom, Ghana's president says the global movement to address the legacy of slavery has reached a "defining moment". 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e3557ba8-28d9-11ef-adee-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000_326P2UC.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e3557ba8-28d9-11ef-adee-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000_326P2UC.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">66eb257c-91aa-11f1-aa99-717baab8f235</guid><pubDate>Mon, 10 Aug 2026 19:01:28 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e3557ba8-28d9-11ef-adee-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000_326P2UC.jpg">AFP - RICARDO MAKYN</source><dc:creator>Zeenat Hansrod</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sports</category><title>Outsiders Malawi beat Ghana to reach WAFCON semi-finals and World Cup</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/sports/20260810-outsiders-malawi-beat-ghana-to-reach-wafcon-semi-finals-and-world-cup</link><description>
Malawi have completed one of the biggest surprises in Women’s Africa Cup of Nations history, coming from behind to beat Ghana 2-1 and secure both a place in the semi-finals and qualification for the 2027 Women’s World Cup.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/6eb2671a-94e4-11f1-b780-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/Malawi-Wafon.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/6eb2671a-94e4-11f1-b780-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/Malawi-Wafon.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">741c5b86-94e2-11f1-b541-a5d0b1ee70af</guid><pubDate>Mon, 10 Aug 2026 17:54:20 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/6eb2671a-94e4-11f1-b780-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/Malawi-Wafon.jpg">© WAFCON</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sports</category><title>EU athletics to apply new TV guidelines on non-sexualisation of women</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/sports/20260810-eu-athletics-comp-to-apply-new-tv-guidelines-on-non-sexualisation-of-women</link><description>
New guidelines to prevent broadcasters sexualising coverage of women athletes will come into place when the European championships start in Birmingham on Monday. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/b7ab3868-114f-11ea-847d-005056a99247/w:1024/p:16x9/2011-10-25T015308Z_1669003487_GM1E7AP0ROS01_RTRMADP_3_GAMES-PANAM.JPG"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/b7ab3868-114f-11ea-847d-005056a99247/w:1024/p:16x9/2011-10-25T015308Z_1669003487_GM1E7AP0ROS01_RTRMADP_3_GAMES-PANAM.JPG" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f8b8b6ae-93d0-11f1-bd75-17f29e945e7d</guid><pubDate>Mon, 10 Aug 2026 09:08:50 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/b7ab3868-114f-11ea-847d-005056a99247/w:1024/p:16x9/2011-10-25T015308Z_1669003487_GM1E7AP0ROS01_RTRMADP_3_GAMES-PANAM.JPG">REUTERS/Desmond Boylan</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Netanyahu rejects Gaza plan in new break from Trump</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260809-netanyahu-rejects-gaza-plan-in-new-break-from-trump</link><description>
Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu on Sunday rejected a US-led Gaza plan endorsed by Hamas, putting distance between himself and President Donald Trump as he tries to shore up his base ahead of close elections.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/4ac69f26-93f2-11f1-862d-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/e9706596eee8ad4dc033e95d5a1ada753b3e6111.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/4ac69f26-93f2-11f1-862d-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/e9706596eee8ad4dc033e95d5a1ada753b3e6111.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4b6eeeec-93f2-11f1-85c5-771bd1b13781</guid><pubDate>Sun, 09 Aug 2026 13:00:27 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/4ac69f26-93f2-11f1-862d-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/e9706596eee8ad4dc033e95d5a1ada753b3e6111.jpg">© Omar AL-QATTAA / AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Environment</category><title>As the planet heats up, butterflies are seeking out cooler climes</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/environment/20260809-as-the-planet-heats-up-butterflies-are-seeking-out-cooler-climes</link><description>
Climate change is driving shifts in where butterflies are found globally, according to a major new study, with some species moving northwards or seeking out higher elevations in search of cooler conditions.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/0ab62654-ab7f-11ed-bf7b-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000_8QJ9J8.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/0ab62654-ab7f-11ed-bf7b-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000_8QJ9J8.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5a42d016-90df-11f1-86ef-872dfaccfb68</guid><pubDate>Sun, 09 Aug 2026 13:39:45 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/0ab62654-ab7f-11ed-bf7b-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000_8QJ9J8.jpg">© AFP - ANDREW BLADON / OXFORD UNIVERSITY</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sports</category><title>Demi Vollering wins Women's Tour de France for the second time</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/sports/20260809-demi-vollering-wins-women-s-tour-de-france-for-the-second-time-cycling</link><description>
Dutch cyclist Demi Vollering on Sunday won her second Women’s Tour de France title, dethroning defending champion Pauline Ferrand-Prévot from France, who dropped out of the race on Saturday. Vollering excelled during the hilly final stage to extend her lead on nearest rival Katarzyna Niewiadoma-Phinney, who finished second overall. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/093aa838-9413-11f1-8ca6-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C4AC6E4.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/093aa838-9413-11f1-8ca6-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C4AC6E4.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">915c12ac-93fe-11f1-945a-49531546ee1a</guid><pubDate>Sun, 09 Aug 2026 17:42:17 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/093aa838-9413-11f1-8ca6-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C4AC6E4.jpg">AFP - NICOLAS TUCAT</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Investigation raises alarm over uranium in DRC cobalt shipments to China</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260809-investigation-raises-alarm-over-uranium-in-drc-cobalt-shipments-to-china</link><description>
An investigation by Lighthouse Reports, The Financial Times and Le Monde traces the possible export of uranium from the Democratic Republic of Congo back to a confidential International Atomic Energy Agency memo obtained in 2024. Chinese mining group CMOC, which owns the main site examined in Katanga, disputes the findings.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/8bc47d66-cce7-11ed-8528-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000_32MK4U2.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/8bc47d66-cce7-11ed-8528-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000_32MK4U2.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a89e4b5e-90a9-11f1-aa9f-076e9a7b708c</guid><pubDate>Sun, 09 Aug 2026 10:53:30 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/8bc47d66-cce7-11ed-8528-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000_32MK4U2.jpg">© AFP/Junior Kannah</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Rise in injuries sees Paris police impose new rules on e-scooter users</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260809-rise-in-injuries-sees-paris-council-impose-new-rules-on-e-scooter-users</link><description>
Electric scooter riders in Paris must now wear helmets and reflective gear under new rules introduced after a significant rise in injuries involving the two-wheelers, police said at the weekend. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/6e326d1e-1654-11ea-9e26-005056a99247/w:1024/p:16x9/971fc82b5aa57ae588c10a511deedf758d068a23.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/6e326d1e-1654-11ea-9e26-005056a99247/w:1024/p:16x9/971fc82b5aa57ae588c10a511deedf758d068a23.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">de1bae24-93d4-11f1-9184-e79cc04984eb</guid><pubDate>Sun, 09 Aug 2026 09:49:22 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/6e326d1e-1654-11ea-9e26-005056a99247/w:1024/p:16x9/971fc82b5aa57ae588c10a511deedf758d068a23.jpg">GETTY/AFP/File</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Sall's chances at UN secretary-general role weakened after first vote</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260809-sall-s-chances-at-un-secretary-general-role-weakened-after-first-vote</link><description>
Antonio Guterres’s successor as United Nations secretary-general will be named in October. So far, two candidates from the African continent – Senegal’s Macky Sall and Uganda’s Olara Otunnu – have failed to win sufficient support.
